\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 02 \'b7 The Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The audit turned up three things that looked like separate problems.\
Asset: 02-1.png; 02-2.png\
Colour hadn't been assigned so much as accumulated. No rule governed what any colour meant. The severity chip (1) held up best: colour-coded with a label, passing AA in both modes, though not AAA. The alert notice (2) and outlined button (3) passed AA in light but failed AA and AAA in dark. The dark value had been set once, by eye, not derived alongside its light counterpart \'97 checked in one mode and shipped in both.\
Asset: 02-3.png\
Icons came from more than one library at more than one size \'97 sharp corners beside rounded ones, a set that read as assembled, not designed.\
All three were the same fault: colour, mode, and iconography decided per screen instead of assigned by role from one library. The product looked assembled, not designed, because that's how it had been decided.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 03 \'b7 Constraints\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Systematizing a changing product.
\f1\b0  The system was built alongside the redesign, not before it, so the rules had to hold for screens still moving.\

\f0\b The system had to be legible to code, not just to designers.
\f1\b0  Variables were going into the codebase as tokens, so the structure had to work for the developers building with it.\

\f0\b Three designers, one system.
\f1\b0  Whatever I built had to work for colleagues immediately, not just me.\

\f0\b Data density was not negotiable.
\f1\b0  The tables hold guards, alerts and threats, everything a responder triages.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 04 \'b7 The Decisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1 \'97 A palette was the start, not the answer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The first move was to define a palette, however, someone still chooses which swatch goes where, and choosing per screen was the actual fault. The palette was raw material, and a semantic layer went on top, defined together with Guardrail's front-end developer. Every token is described by where it\'92s used (surface, component, input), what it's for (primary, secondary, plain, positive, warning, negative), how much attention it draws (high, medium, low saliency), how it's applied (background, border, text, icon), and its state. A full path might read 
\f3\fs26 component / secondary / high / background / default
\f1\fs24  \'97 the default background for a CTA in the secondary brand colour, weighted to draw the eye first.\
Asset: 04-1-1.png; 04-1-2.png; 04-1-3.png\
Mode became a further axis of the same taxonomy, not a separate pass. Every token holds a light and dark value defined and checked together. Each value is verified against AA, so a failing token is caught before it reaches a screen.\
The cost is that the taxonomy has to be learned before it can be used: five dimensions, long names, and a designer who wants one colour has to answer several questions to get it. Harder to use casually, much harder to use incorrectly. AAA was the aim on text, but reaching 7:1 would have narrowed the palette, so some settled for AA instead, keeping the range the product needed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 2 \'97 Two views, not one\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The received answer for a dense table on a small screen is to replace it with stacked cards or hidden columns. I kept the table, horizontal scroll and all, and added a list view beside it.\
Asset: 04-2-1.mov\
Tables exist because comparison across columns is the task. Collapse it and you've removed what the table was for, not made it mobile. But at phone width a table is genuinely hard to read, so the list view covers other needs that aren\'92t comparison.\
Asset: 04-2-2.png; 04-2-3.png; 04-2-4.png\
The cost is two views to maintain, and a decision the viewer now has to make, minimized by the breakpoints:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
